// Drowned Belfry layout (WP-061): greybox blocks (scaled `block_unit`, centered on `pos`). Y is
// up; the ground is terrain.ron's 0 m, with one pit: the bell shaft. 6 m walls, 2 m thick.
// Rooms (interior rectangles, x then z):
//   A   Landing          x -12..12   z -76..-56   the stair up to Mirrormere (south gap), L07 outside
//   T1  Bell Chamber     x -12..12   z -54..-32   the teaching room: bell A, one Husk; door_t1 opens by the bell
//   G   Choir Gallery    x -16..16   z -30..-6    the test room: bell B stuns the choir; door_g opens by it
//   S   Side Chapel      x -34..-18  z -22..-10   the branch: the Greatanchor; a hollow wall hides closet C
//   C   Secret closet    x -42..-36  z -18..-14   Mirror Ward
//   TH  Tide Hall        x -16..16   z  -4..22    the twist: a dry causeway between two deep channels of Drowned
//   K   Bell shaft       x  18..34   z   0..18    a 12 m well; the lift's top stop is the doorway (x 17), the
//                        Hollowdeep exit at the bottom; door_shaft opens when bell C rings
//   LO  Belfry Loft      x -16..16   z  24..52    the elite: the Choir Knight, bell D, the sluice lever, Choir Litany
//   R   Return           corridor from the loft's east door (x 17, z 36..40), east to x 42..46, south to
